Whenever I play this game, there is a steady and upward trend in the
number of items in the game.  Most levels with anything interesting will
have huge piles of old armor, weapons, loot, etc.  In 3.0 this was no
problem, you just leave them lying around and take what you want.  In
3.1 the monsters can take what you leave behind, and soon every monster
has low AC and a decent weapon.  

What can you do to get rid of all this blasted equipment?  It is a lot
easier to clean up the level than leave stuff for baddies to find and
use.  I'm not so concerned about using it, rather just neutralizing it.

Here's my list...

1) Throw it in a pool.
2) Put it in a pile.  Push a boulder on top of it.
3) Polypile it (note: I never have WoP.  The only 3.1 game I ascended 
didn't even generate one until the last level of the endgame)
4) Polymorph into something else and eat it. (see 3)
5) Sell it to a shopkeeper.
6) Leave it in a pile with a scroll of scare monster/Elbereth.
7) Put it in a closet + lock the door.
8) Find a nasty trap (sleep gas + spiked pit come to mind) and leave it
there.
9) Put it in a chest.
10) (wands only) Make sure you've exhausted all charges before pitching.
11) (weapons only) Engrave with them to dull them and give them a big 
penalty for monsters who try to use them.

Any other ideas?  I find 2 and 9 most convenient, since most levels have
at least one boulder or chest on them, and it lets me get the items back
later if I want them.  

